# .nbi.ff = non-bonded interaction (per-atom-type charge/radius/epsilon/mass/
# transfer-energy parameters -- steric, electrostatic, hydrophobicity, IMP).
# Identical duplicate of the .ff file of the same name, kept only for
# backward compatibility with --ff/--grp: the newer .nbi.ff/.bi.ff pair of
# extensions distinguishes non-bonded (.nbi.ff, this file) from bonded
# (.bi.ff -- stretching/bending/[future dihedral] springs retuned onto a
# --rigidbody topology, see BondedForceFieldReader) parameter files.
#
#type	charge(e)	radius(A)	epsilon(kJ.mol-1)	mass(Da)	transferIMP(kJ.mol-1.A-2	Hydrophobicity(sqrt(kJ.mol-1.A-1))
# NOTE: the Hydrophobicity column is 0 for every type here, so the pairwise
# hydrophobic term is inert with this force field -- which is the state every
# force field shipped with BioSpring was in. The column is written out
# explicitly rather than omitted, so that "no hydrophobicity" is something
# the file says rather than something the reader infers.
ABB	0.00	4.7	0.000	72.0000	0.0137	0.0
ASC1	0.00	4.1	0.000	54.0000	-0.0303	0.0
RBB	0.00	4.7	0.000	72.0000	0.0137	0.0
